{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":39,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["To the chief Musician, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["even"]}," to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 39:1"},"I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 39:2"},"I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["even"]}," from good; and my sorrow was stirred. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 39:3"},"My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["then"]}," spake I with my tongue, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 39:4"},"LORD, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is; that"]}," I may know how frail I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am."]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 39:5"},"Behold, thou hast made my days ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," an handbreadth; and mine age ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," altogether vanity. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 39:6"},"Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["riches,"]}," and knoweth not who shall gather them. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 39:7"},"And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," in thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 39:8"},"Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 39:9"},"I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 39:10"},"Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:10"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PSA 39:11"},"When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," vanity. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:11"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PSA 39:12"},"Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," a stranger with thee, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," a sojourner, as all my fathers ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["were."]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:12"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PSA 39:13"},"O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 39:13"}]}]}
